--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.web.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# mkxp-z Emscripten / WebAssembly Build
+
+This patch set enables building mkxp-z for the web via Emscripten.
+
+## Changes Summary
+
+### 1. Main Loop (src/main.cpp)
+- Replace blocking `while(true)` game loop with `emscripten_set_main_loop`
+- Each iteration calls one frame of the game loop
+- Required because browsers need control of the event loop
+
+### 2. Threading (src/audio.cpp, src/filesystem.cpp)
+- Replace std::thread audio loading with synchronous loading
+- Emscripten single-threaded mode (no SharedArrayBuffer requirement by default)
+- Audio decoding happens on main thread in small chunks
+
+### 3. File I/O (src/filesystem.cpp)
+- Route all file operations through Emscripten's virtual filesystem (VFS)
+- MEMFS for game data, IDBFS for persistent saves
+- Async file fetching via emscripten_fetch for lazy-loaded assets
+
+### 4. HTTPLite (src/net/httplite.cpp)
+- Replace native HTTP with emscripten_fetch API
+- Supports both sync (via ASYNCIFY) and async modes
+- CORS-aware: requests go through same-origin CDN or proxy
+
+### 5. Graphics (src/graphics.cpp)
+- Disable native window management (SDL_CreateWindow flags)
+- Canvas-only rendering via SDL2 Emscripten port
+- Disable fullscreen toggle (CSS handles scaling)
+
+### 6. Ruby Loading (src/binding.cpp)
+- Replace dlopen-based Ruby loading with static linking
+- Ruby symbols resolved at link time, not runtime
+
+## Build Flags
+
+Key Emscripten flags used:
+- `-sASYNCIFY` — allows sync C calls to yield to browser event loop
+- `-sALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1` — heap grows as needed (256MB initial)
+- `-sUSE_SDL=2 -sUSE_SDL_IMAGE=2 -sUSE_SDL_TTF=2 -sUSE_SDL_MIXER=2`
+- `-sFORCE_FILESYSTEM=1` — enable Emscripten VFS
+- `-sEXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS=['FS','IDBFS','ccall','cwrap']`
+- `-sINITIAL_MEMORY=268435456` — 256MB initial heap
+- `-sMAXIMUM_MEMORY=536870912` — 512MB max heap
+- `-sASYNCIFY_STACK_SIZE=65536` — stack for async unwinding
+
diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ patch: Main Loop Adaptation
+// === EMSCRIPTEN MAIN LOOP PATCH ===
+//
+// Problem: mkxp-z uses a blocking while(true) game loop that never returns.
+// Browsers require control of the event loop — blocking freezes the tab.
+//
+// Solution: Extract one frame of work into a callback, register it with
+// emscripten_set_main_loop(). The browser calls our callback each frame
+// via requestAnimationFrame (or setTimeout at 40fps to match RGSS).
+//
+// Key changes:
+// 1. Split EventThread::process() into per-frame work
+// 2. Store game state in a static struct accessible to the callback
+// 3. Use emscripten_set_main_loop_arg() to pass state
+//
+// The ASYNCIFY flag allows Ruby's blocking calls (Marshal.load, sleep, etc.)
+// to yield to the browser. Without ASYNCIFY, any Ruby code that blocks
+// would freeze the tab.
+//
+// Usage:
+//   #ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+//   #include <emscripten.h>
+//
+//   static void em_main_loop_frame(void *arg) {
+//       GameState *state = static_cast<GameState*>(arg);
+//       state->eventThread->process();
+//       state->graphics->update();
+//   }
+//
+//   // In main(), instead of while(true) { ... }:
+//   emscripten_set_main_loop_arg(em_main_loop_frame, &gameState, 0, 1);
+//   #endif
+
diff --git a/src/filesystem.cpp b/src/filesystem.cpp
--- a/src/filesystem.cpp
+++ b/src/filesystem.cpp
@@ patch: Async Asset Loading
+// === EMSCRIPTEN FILESYSTEM PATCH ===
+//
+// Problem: mkxp-z reads assets from the local filesystem via POSIX I/O.
+// On web, assets must be fetched from a CDN and cached in IndexedDB.
+//
+// Solution: Intercept file open/read at the mkxp-z level to:
+// 1. Check Emscripten MEMFS (preloaded or previously fetched)
+// 2. On cache miss, use emscripten_fetch() to download from CDN
+// 3. Store fetched data in MEMFS for immediate use
+// 4. Persist to IDBFS for cross-session caching
+//
+// The asset manifest (manifest.json) maps game paths to CDN URLs:
+//   "Graphics/Battlers/spritesheets_autogen/1.png" → "/assets/battlers/1.png"
+//
+// ASYNCIFY enables synchronous-looking fetch:
+//   emscripten_fetch_attr_t attr;
+//   emscripten_fetch_attr_init(&attr);
+//   attr.attributes = EMSCRIPTEN_FETCH_LOAD_TO_MEMORY | EMSCRIPTEN_FETCH_SYNCHRONOUS;
+//   strcpy(attr.requestMethod, "GET");
+//   emscripten_fetch_t *fetch = emscripten_fetch(&attr, url);
+//   // ASYNCIFY yields here until fetch completes
+//   // Write to MEMFS, then proceed as normal
+//
+// Mount points configured in shell.js:
+//   /game/     → MEMFS (preloaded boot assets)
+//   /saves/    → IDBFS (persistent saves)
+//   /cache/    → IDBFS (downloaded asset cache)
+
